{"duration_ms":0,"id":25,"kind":"llm","model":"claude-opus-5","name":"claude-code.turn.16","provider":"anthropic","response":{"content":[{"text":"`'urgent,'` is gone, and no empty tags leak through.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `normalise.py:6` — `clean_token` now strips commas (along with whitespace) from both ends. Its docstring previously promised to \"drop punctuation\" but never did; I narrowed the docstring to what the function actually guarantees rather than stripping punctuation broadly, which would have mangled legitimate tags like `c++` and `node.js` (verified intact above).\n- `csv_import.py` / `form_import.py` — filter on the *normalized* value instead of the raw part, so a token that is only a comma drops out instead of becoming `''`.\n\n**Two things worth flagging**\n\n1. The `'urgent,'` tag was not coming from the CSV importer. `tags_from_csv` splits on `,`, so trailing commas were already absorbed by the delimiter. The producer is `tags_from_form`, which splits on whitespace — someone typed `urgent, ops` into the form field. The fix lives in the shared `clean_token`, so it covers both paths regardless, but if you were tracking this to a CSV file, that's the wrong trail.\n\n2. Separately, `tags_from_csv` is a naive `split(\",\")` with no quote handling, so a quoted field like `\"urgent,\"` still parses as two junk tags:\n   ```\n   tags_from_csv('bug, \"urgent,\" ,ops') -> ['bug', '\"urgent', '\"', 'ops']\n   ```\n   That's a distinct bug from the one you asked about and needs `csv.reader` rather than `split`. I left it alone — say the word if you want it fixed.","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_011CeuKpX4GsvcQ4JSVxWK2x","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":523},"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":20644,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"start_ms":0,"usage":{"cache_read":20644,"cache_write_5m":523,"input":2,"output":1}}
